{
  "name": "Occult Association: Kabbalist (Tier 4)",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Tier 4 — Kabbalist</strong></p><p><strong>“You don’t cleanse a Hex. You convince it to remember what it was meant to be.”</strong></p><p>At Tier 4, you are no longer merely a reader of alignment. You are a <em>shifter</em>. When your faction pushes a Hex toward a Sephirah, you can feel where the resistance is and where to apply pressure so the world gives way instead of breaking.</p><p><strong>Strategic (Faction Scale)</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Alignment Authority:</strong> when your faction attempts to shift a Hex’s alignment toward a Sephirah, choose one:</li><ul><li>gain <strong>Advantage</strong> on the Opposed Strategic Roll, <em>or</em></li><li>reduce the OP cost of the shift by <strong>10%</strong> (minimum reduction 1 OP when spending 10+ OP; otherwise GM adjudicates)</li></ul></ul><p><em>The Tree hears you more clearly than it hears most people.</em></p><p><strong>Cost:</strong> forced alignment is never free. Expect backlash, revealed contradictions, metaphysical strain, or nearby instability when you make the world remember too quickly.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
